Subject: [PATCH 066/154] feat(atrium): insecure-origin treatment on whichever
 address bar is showing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ported from the lab: red ground, dark red ink, an inset ring, the broken padlock,
the words Not secure, and the host. Only the insecure state prints the host - the
secure sidebar bar keeps its placeholder, because that bar has no url of its own.

The ink race needed care. renderSidebar rebuilds the bar on every push, so the
security check sits in buildUrlBar at construction rather than only in a live
update - a space-switch rebuild then paints red on its first frame instead of
racing the theme ink. Checking for a live per-frame ink push found none: no
atriumSetSidebarInk exists and --fg is never set, so an inline colour closes the
race as things stand.

The localhost rule is the lab's, and the lab never covers 127.0.0.1 or [::1], so
those are flagged Not secure today. Ported rather than widened on purpose, and
tracked separately, because the Rust core already solved this properly after
three rounds of hardening.

grit's ID allocation for the grd needed raising to fit the new module.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
index c9c488f5019ff..ff404801ac217 100644
--- a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
+++ b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
@@ -1810,7 +1810,7 @@
   # Atrium chrome layer. Placed at the end of this section so the
   # real IDs land after the placeholder block and nothing downstream realigns.
   "chrome/browser/resources/atrium/atrium_resources.grd": {
-    "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [60]}},
+    "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [70]}},
     "includes": [12020],
   },
 
